"Morwenna loved Kerra Pascoe, a net-maker's daughter, who sailed south four years ago and married."
"Kerra never knew; Morwenna watched her ship out from the gallery and has told no one since."
"Morwenna fears being left above all, and pushes people off before they can leave her."
"On the night Nala came, Morwenna asked the lamp aloud for someone who would stay."
